1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:04,003
[microphone feedback]

2
00:00:04,004 --> 00:00:06,006
[♪ opening theme music playing]

3
00:00:40,541 --> 00:00:44,043
FLEX X COP 2

4
00:00:44,044 --> 00:00:46,879
CHARACTERS, PLACES, ORGANIZATIONS,
AND EVENTS IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

5
00:00:46,880 --> 00:00:48,966
ALL CHILD ACTORS AND ANIMALS
FILMED IN A SAFE ENVIRONMENT

6
00:00:53,553 --> 00:00:55,471
- Thank you for the meal.
- Thank you.

7
00:00:55,472 --> 00:00:57,181
[eatery owner] Thank you, bye.

8
00:00:57,182 --> 00:00:58,684
[shop bell chimes, door opens]

9
00:00:59,434 --> 00:01:01,019
[door closes, shop bell chimes]

10
00:01:03,021 --> 00:01:04,439
EPISODE 7

11
00:01:05,023 --> 00:01:07,692
Ah! [chuckles softly]

12
00:01:07,693 --> 00:01:09,235
It's been a while.

13
00:01:09,236 --> 00:01:10,444
It has.

14
00:01:10,445 --> 00:01:12,072
I missed your <i>gukbap.</i>

15
00:01:16,868 --> 00:01:19,496
By the way, I don't see your wife.

16
00:01:20,539 --> 00:01:23,166
She passed last year.

17
00:01:24,334 --> 00:01:25,835
[♪ gentle, melancholy music playing]

18
00:01:25,836 --> 00:01:28,963
She said she just wanted to know

19
00:01:28,964 --> 00:01:30,716
whether our son was alive or not.

20
00:01:31,925 --> 00:01:33,302
I wonder if she knows now.

21
00:01:39,141 --> 00:01:40,142
[exhales softly]

22
00:01:41,810 --> 00:01:43,145
Even now, sometimes,

23
00:01:44,313 --> 00:01:46,523
Heejun appears in my dreams.

24
00:01:48,358 --> 00:01:50,068
He's probably dead.

25
00:01:55,532 --> 00:01:56,783
Please find him.

26
00:02:01,330 --> 00:02:02,914
So I can at least hold a funeral.

27
00:02:05,709 --> 00:02:06,710
[sighs softly]

28
00:02:18,347 --> 00:02:19,847
[Changun] Joo Hyera.

29
00:02:19,848 --> 00:02:20,974
[♪ music fades]

30
00:02:27,606 --> 00:02:28,607
[sighs softly]

31
00:02:30,567 --> 00:02:31,568
Got a lot on your mind?

32
00:02:37,949 --> 00:02:39,367
Are you still after Yu Seongwon?

33
00:02:39,368 --> 00:02:42,244
YU SEONGWON RETURNS AFTER 4 YEARS
TO HOLD A SOLO EXHIBITION

34
00:02:42,245 --> 00:02:44,914
That's why you came back here, isn't it?

35
00:02:44,915 --> 00:02:47,208
[♪ soft, suspenseful music playing]

36
00:02:47,209 --> 00:02:48,751
I know how you feel.

37
00:02:48,752 --> 00:02:51,128
There's always that one case
we can't forget.

38
00:02:51,129 --> 00:02:52,630
But

39
00:02:52,631 --> 00:02:54,466
we checked Yu Seongwon's alibi.

40
00:02:59,846 --> 00:03:01,390
It's become an obsession for you.

41
00:03:02,015 --> 00:03:03,140
Huh?

42
00:03:03,141 --> 00:03:04,725
That's what ruins detectives.

43
00:03:04,726 --> 00:03:06,311
It's not an obsession.

44
00:03:07,688 --> 00:03:08,730
Yu Seongwon

45
00:03:10,399 --> 00:03:11,983
will kill again.

46
00:03:13,235 --> 00:03:14,611
I'm going to stop him.

47
00:03:20,659 --> 00:03:21,868
[♪ music fades]

48
00:03:32,087 --> 00:03:33,839
[♪ ominous music playing]

49
00:04:01,116 --> 00:04:03,743
DISSOLUTION
THE SILENCE OF WHISPERING REEDS

50
00:04:07,122 --> 00:04:09,374
[♪ music increases in tempo]

51
00:04:27,726 --> 00:04:28,977
[♪ music swells]

52
00:04:36,485 --> 00:04:37,610
[Isoo] Seongwon.

53
00:04:37,611 --> 00:04:38,612
[♪ music stops]

54
00:04:39,237 --> 00:04:40,321
[Seongwon] Isoo!

55
00:04:40,322 --> 00:04:42,115
- Oh!
- [chuckles]

56
00:04:43,033 --> 00:04:45,910
[grunts] I really missed you.

57
00:04:45,911 --> 00:04:47,077
[Isoo] Me too.

58
00:04:47,078 --> 00:04:50,247
Hey, this is for you.
I've never given flowers to a guy before.

59
00:04:50,248 --> 00:04:51,666
[Seongwon chuckles]

60
00:04:52,250 --> 00:04:55,795
Whoa, you're looking
even better than before.

61
00:04:55,796 --> 00:04:56,921
It's nothing new.

62
00:04:56,922 --> 00:05:00,216
Hey, you're finally starting to look
like a professional artist now.

63
00:05:00,217 --> 00:05:01,509
- Really?
- Yeah.

64
00:05:01,510 --> 00:05:02,593
- [chuckles]
- [sighs]

65
00:05:02,594 --> 00:05:03,929
Just look at all this.

66
00:05:05,180 --> 00:05:07,139
Isoo, come this way.

67
00:05:07,140 --> 00:05:09,058
- You need to see this piece first.
- What?

68
00:05:09,059 --> 00:05:10,811
[♪ tense suspenseful music playing]

69
00:05:18,026 --> 00:05:19,319
[♪ music fades]

70
00:05:20,487 --> 00:05:22,488
SEOUL GANGHA POLICE STATION

71
00:05:22,489 --> 00:05:23,907
All right.

72
00:05:25,534 --> 00:05:27,993
Look closely. Nothing here, right?

73
00:05:27,994 --> 00:05:29,161
No, nothing there.

74
00:05:29,162 --> 00:05:30,705
Put your hand in and feel it.

75
00:05:32,624 --> 00:05:34,708
- There's really nothing here.
- Nothing there.

76
00:05:34,709 --> 00:05:38,254
And if I mix in a bit of magic
from Kyungjin's nose...

77
00:05:38,255 --> 00:05:40,507
[exclaims, whispers] Now, let's see.

78
00:05:41,716 --> 00:05:43,760
[grunts] Oh my gosh.

79
00:05:44,928 --> 00:05:46,220
Ta-da.

80
00:05:46,221 --> 00:05:47,596
Ooh, how did you do that?

81
00:05:47,597 --> 00:05:49,139
There's a secret compartment.

82
00:05:49,140 --> 00:05:51,308
I expected a rabbit at the very least.

83
00:05:51,309 --> 00:05:54,186
[scoffs] Hey, see if there's
a secret compartment.

84
00:05:54,187 --> 00:05:55,188
As if.

85
00:05:59,150 --> 00:06:01,443
All right, in here,

86
00:06:01,444 --> 00:06:03,697
add a bit of magic from Jin Isoo's nose,

87
00:06:05,240 --> 00:06:07,324
- and voilà.
- Whoa!

88
00:06:07,325 --> 00:06:09,910
So anyone can do this.

89
00:06:09,911 --> 00:06:11,079
[scoffs softly]

90
00:06:11,329 --> 00:06:12,621
How did you know?

91
00:06:12,622 --> 00:06:15,291
It's obvious.
It's not like you have a magic pocket.

92
00:06:15,292 --> 00:06:17,418
You're such a killjoy.

93
00:06:17,419 --> 00:06:18,670
You told me to try.

94
00:06:20,589 --> 00:06:21,798
Bro.

95
00:06:22,674 --> 00:06:23,966
Park Jaeha's magic show.

96
00:06:23,967 --> 00:06:25,509
These tickets are impossible to get.

97
00:06:25,510 --> 00:06:28,012
You said you wanted to see it.
Those are VIP seats.

98
00:06:28,013 --> 00:06:29,346
What is it?

99
00:06:29,347 --> 00:06:30,472
[♪ jaunty music playing]

100
00:06:30,473 --> 00:06:33,350
Magic is basically deception, isn't it?

101
00:06:33,351 --> 00:06:34,727
[scoffs]

102
00:06:34,728 --> 00:06:36,145
Deception?

103
00:06:36,146 --> 00:06:38,022
Magic is an art.

104
00:06:38,023 --> 00:06:41,150
An elevated art form
where science meets performance.

105
00:06:41,151 --> 00:06:42,234
I'm not interested.

106
00:06:42,235 --> 00:06:44,361
Really? I have a ticket for Dr. Yoon, too.

107
00:06:44,362 --> 00:06:46,740
Really? Then I'll go. Thanks.

108
00:06:47,657 --> 00:06:49,784
- You bring your girlfriend, too.
- Thanks, bro.

109
00:06:52,871 --> 00:06:56,082
You can throw it away or use it
as scrap paper if you don't need it.

110
00:06:57,292 --> 00:06:58,876
I'm coming, too.

111
00:06:58,877 --> 00:06:59,961
Really?

112
00:07:00,587 --> 00:07:02,589
If you really want it, be my guest.

113
00:07:05,091 --> 00:07:06,134
[♪ music fades]

114
00:07:10,013 --> 00:07:11,640
[♪ upbeat, jaunty music playing]

115
00:07:13,058 --> 00:07:14,601
Oh, Detective Jin.

116
00:07:15,393 --> 00:07:16,560
Hey...

117
00:07:16,561 --> 00:07:19,063
Thanks for the ticket.
I really wanted to see this.

118
00:07:19,064 --> 00:07:21,650
Ah, I knew you were
a cultured person, Dr. Yoon.

119
00:07:22,275 --> 00:07:24,861
- What about me?
- You're just a person.

120
00:07:25,445 --> 00:07:26,655
[chuckles softly]

121
00:07:27,530 --> 00:07:28,947
[Dr. Yoon] Detective Joo.

122
00:07:28,948 --> 00:07:30,783
You look great today.

123
00:07:30,784 --> 00:07:32,785
Ah. [chuckles] Not at all.

124
00:07:32,786 --> 00:07:34,078
You look great, too.

125
00:07:34,079 --> 00:07:35,205
[chuckles softly]

126
00:07:36,623 --> 00:07:37,706
You look awful.

127
00:07:37,707 --> 00:07:38,875
Yeah, you too.

128
00:07:40,001 --> 00:07:41,210
Why is he so late?

129
00:07:41,211 --> 00:07:44,129
[sighs] I've never met
Kyungjin's girlfriend before.

130
00:07:44,130 --> 00:07:45,756
Me neither.

131
00:07:45,757 --> 00:07:48,676
Don't tease him
when his girlfriend arrives.

132
00:07:48,677 --> 00:07:51,512
When do we ever tease? We congratulate.

133
00:07:51,513 --> 00:07:52,597
[chuckles]

134
00:07:53,348 --> 00:07:54,391
[Kyungjin] Bro!

135
00:07:55,725 --> 00:07:57,726
Why are you alone?
Where's your girlfriend?

136
00:07:57,727 --> 00:07:58,894
She has to work late today.

137
00:07:58,895 --> 00:08:00,312
- Out of the blue?
- Yeah.

138
00:08:00,313 --> 00:08:02,357
She wanted to come,
but she's been busy lately.

139
00:08:03,858 --> 00:08:05,442
Too bad, then.

140
00:08:05,443 --> 00:08:06,903
Shall we head inside?

141
00:08:08,822 --> 00:08:10,489
[Isoo] You don't have a girlfriend,
do you?

142
00:08:10,490 --> 00:08:11,573
[Kyungjin] I do.

143
00:08:11,574 --> 00:08:13,201
- [Isoo] I don't think you do.
- [Kyungjin] I really do.

144
00:08:14,119 --> 00:08:16,079
[♪ upbeat, intriguing music playing]

145
00:08:32,929 --> 00:08:34,763
[♪ music slows]

146
00:08:34,764 --> 00:08:36,306
[♪ music resumes tempo]

147
00:08:36,307 --> 00:08:38,226
[audience cheering, applauding]

148
00:08:45,650 --> 00:08:49,695
[announcer] <i>And now,
Park Jaeha's Magic Fire begins!</i>

149
00:08:49,696 --> 00:08:51,781
[audience continues cheering, applauding]

150
00:09:31,237 --> 00:09:32,489
Ooh!

151
00:09:35,325 --> 00:09:36,993
[♪ music slows]

152
00:09:37,952 --> 00:09:39,621
[♪ music resumes tempo]

153
00:09:40,705 --> 00:09:41,956
[flames whooshing]

154
00:09:44,751 --> 00:09:45,835
[audience gasps]

155
00:09:48,379 --> 00:09:50,172
[audience exclaims in amazement]

156
00:09:50,173 --> 00:09:51,257
[Isoo] Whoa!

157
00:09:51,841 --> 00:09:53,551
[softly] How did he light it on fire?

158
00:09:54,302 --> 00:09:56,095
[whispering] Hey, have some manners.
[clicks tongue]

159
00:09:56,096 --> 00:09:58,055
I want to know what the trick is.

160
00:09:58,056 --> 00:10:00,140
It's not a trick. It's art.

161
00:10:00,141 --> 00:10:01,518
What's the matter with you?

162
00:10:02,519 --> 00:10:04,437
[successive electrical thuds echoing]

163
00:10:05,730 --> 00:10:07,357
[♪ gentle piano music playing]

164
00:10:13,780 --> 00:10:16,908
There is someone I love.

165
00:10:26,751 --> 00:10:28,293
She lived an unhappy life,

166
00:10:28,294 --> 00:10:31,339
because her father was a violent man.

167
00:10:32,132 --> 00:10:33,216
[sighs wearily]

168
00:10:35,885 --> 00:10:37,428
[♪ dramatic sting]

169
00:10:38,054 --> 00:10:39,055
I wanted

170
00:10:40,932 --> 00:10:42,392
to make her smile.

171
00:11:07,375 --> 00:11:09,252
[♪ enchanting music playing]

172
00:11:10,503 --> 00:11:11,795
- [audience exclaims in awe]
- Oh...

173
00:11:11,796 --> 00:11:12,880
What on earth?

174
00:11:12,881 --> 00:11:14,465
- Whoa!
- Whoa.

175
00:11:22,765 --> 00:11:24,350
[♪ music increases in tempo]

176
00:11:54,505 --> 00:11:55,548
[gasps softly]

177
00:12:07,143 --> 00:12:09,062
[♪ music swells]

178
00:12:15,735 --> 00:12:16,945
[♪ music fades]

179
00:12:17,737 --> 00:12:19,447
[♪ upbeat, lively
orchestral music playing]

180
00:12:38,216 --> 00:12:39,592
[audience exclaims in amazement]

181
00:12:46,557 --> 00:12:47,809
[audience applauding]

182
00:12:57,068 --> 00:12:58,403
[♪ music fades]

183
00:13:03,032 --> 00:13:04,784
[♪ gentle piano music playing]

184
00:13:31,144 --> 00:13:33,688
- [audience exclaims in awe]
- [Isoo] Whoa.

185
00:13:34,647 --> 00:13:36,441
[♪ enchanting music playing]

186
00:13:55,668 --> 00:13:57,502
[audience exclaims in awe]

187
00:13:57,503 --> 00:13:58,588
Where is he going?

188
00:14:22,195 --> 00:14:23,446
[♪ music fades]

189
00:14:24,447 --> 00:14:25,740
[gunshot]

190
00:14:29,702 --> 00:14:31,119
- Oh!
- [audience gasps]

191
00:14:31,120 --> 00:14:32,955
[♪ gentle piano music playing]

192
00:14:40,129 --> 00:14:41,506
[breath trembling]

193
00:14:42,924 --> 00:14:44,049
[flames whoosh]

194
00:14:44,050 --> 00:14:45,884
[audience gasps in shock]

195
00:14:45,885 --> 00:14:47,637
- [scattered screams]
- [♪ music fades]

196
00:14:48,596 --> 00:14:50,055
Whoa...

197
00:14:50,056 --> 00:14:51,431
Oh!

198
00:14:51,432 --> 00:14:52,517
[Junyoung] Wow.

199
00:14:53,643 --> 00:14:55,061
[fire roaring]

200
00:14:57,021 --> 00:14:58,147
[breathes shakily]

201
00:15:01,192 --> 00:15:03,360
- [flames whoosh, roar intensely]
- [audience gasps in horror]

202
00:15:03,361 --> 00:15:05,154
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

203
00:15:07,740 --> 00:15:09,450
- [burning wood crashes]
- [partner screams]

204
00:15:09,867 --> 00:15:11,077
[screaming in horror]

205
00:15:13,663 --> 00:15:14,913
Help!

206
00:15:14,914 --> 00:15:16,499
[audience exclaiming in horror]

207
00:15:17,917 --> 00:15:20,085
- Get everyone to safety first.
- Okay.

208
00:15:20,086 --> 00:15:22,337
Help! Oh my god!

209
00:15:22,338 --> 00:15:25,924
[Isoo] Everyone, it's all right.
Remain calm and follow our instructions.

210
00:15:25,925 --> 00:15:29,303
[Junyoung] Everyone, please slow down.
Please evacuate in an orderly manner.

211
00:15:30,304 --> 00:15:31,930
- [clamoring]
- Please walk slowly.

212
00:15:31,931 --> 00:15:34,392
Please evacuate in an orderly manner.

213
00:15:40,481 --> 00:15:41,649
[♪ music fades]

214
00:15:42,775 --> 00:15:45,193
[Changun, over phone]
<i>So you're saying that magician is dead?</i>

215
00:15:45,194 --> 00:15:47,905
Yes, he died in a fire
during the performance.

216
00:15:48,573 --> 00:15:49,657
[sighs wearily]

217
00:15:50,324 --> 00:15:52,784
I'll send forensics over.
Your team will take this case.

218
00:15:52,785 --> 00:15:54,328
Yes, sir.

219
00:15:54,912 --> 00:15:55,996
[line disconnects]

220
00:15:55,997 --> 00:15:57,748
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

221
00:16:00,668 --> 00:16:02,752
How could something like this happen?

222
00:16:02,753 --> 00:16:04,005
I know.

223
00:16:07,717 --> 00:16:09,093
We're taking this case.

224
00:16:10,094 --> 00:16:13,097
If you need an autopsy, let me know.

225
00:16:13,764 --> 00:16:14,849
I'm going to go.

226
00:16:15,600 --> 00:16:16,601
I'll leave you to it.

227
00:16:20,438 --> 00:16:22,272
Let's get statements from people first.

228
00:16:22,273 --> 00:16:23,274
- Got it.
- [Kyungjin] Got it.

229
00:16:26,986 --> 00:16:28,029
[Isoo] Hmm...

230
00:16:32,658 --> 00:16:33,742
Is he...

231
00:16:33,743 --> 00:16:35,702
MAGIC PERFORMANCE PARTNER
JEONG DAHEE

232
00:16:35,703 --> 00:16:37,413
[voice shaking] Is he really dead?

233
00:16:41,459 --> 00:16:42,460
Yes.

234
00:16:44,086 --> 00:16:47,506
[sobbing] How could he die like this?

235
00:16:48,382 --> 00:16:49,717
[sniffling, sobbing]

236
00:16:54,013 --> 00:16:56,807
How long have you
worked with Mr. Park Jaeha?

237
00:16:58,142 --> 00:17:00,102
From a year ago.

238
00:17:00,853 --> 00:17:03,563
So, earlier,

239
00:17:03,564 --> 00:17:05,274
what happened to the casket?

240
00:17:06,234 --> 00:17:07,610
I don't know.

241
00:17:08,527 --> 00:17:10,737
[breath trembling] Originally,

242
00:17:10,738 --> 00:17:14,074
it was supposed to open from the back.

243
00:17:14,075 --> 00:17:15,493
[♪ intriguing music playing]

244
00:17:18,037 --> 00:17:20,830
And then he's supposed to reappear.

245
00:17:20,831 --> 00:17:22,375
[♪ music increases in tempo]

246
00:17:29,090 --> 00:17:30,550
[♪ music swells]

247
00:17:36,931 --> 00:17:38,057
[audience applauding]

248
00:17:39,559 --> 00:17:40,725
[♪ music fades]

249
00:17:40,726 --> 00:17:44,564
[sobbing] I don't know how this happened.

250
00:17:45,356 --> 00:17:46,357
[Isoo sighs softly]

251
00:17:47,024 --> 00:17:48,025
[Hyera sighs]

252
00:17:48,818 --> 00:17:50,819
[♪ tense pulsating music playing]

253
00:17:50,820 --> 00:17:52,321
[camera shutter clicking]

254
00:18:01,163 --> 00:18:03,666
What could have happened here?

255
00:18:04,792 --> 00:18:06,001
[voice shaking] I don't know.

256
00:18:06,002 --> 00:18:08,087
STAGE DIRECTOR
LEE JIYUN

257
00:18:09,088 --> 00:18:10,171
[sniffles]

258
00:18:10,172 --> 00:18:12,757
The escape mechanism worked just fine.

259
00:18:12,758 --> 00:18:14,302
He should've come down this way.

260
00:18:17,888 --> 00:18:20,099
Could there have been
a problem with the casket?

261
00:18:20,933 --> 00:18:23,560
I checked everything just before the show.

262
00:18:23,561 --> 00:18:25,353
There was nothing wrong with it.

263
00:18:25,354 --> 00:18:26,771
[♪ music swells]

264
00:18:26,772 --> 00:18:27,857
[sobbing]

265
00:18:30,901 --> 00:18:31,944
[♪ music fades]

266
00:18:32,570 --> 00:18:33,613
[Kyungjin] Detective Joo!

267
00:18:35,615 --> 00:18:37,074
The escape mechanism was working.

268
00:18:37,992 --> 00:18:40,118
Then was something wrong with the casket?

269
00:18:40,119 --> 00:18:42,621
The stage director said
nothing was wrong with it.

270
00:18:42,622 --> 00:18:43,913
Who made the casket?

271
00:18:43,914 --> 00:18:45,165
An engineer made it.

272
00:18:45,166 --> 00:18:46,666
His workshop is right next door.

273
00:18:46,667 --> 00:18:48,710
Mmm. We'll go meet him.

274
00:18:48,711 --> 00:18:50,421
Okay. I'll check the security cameras.

275
00:18:54,634 --> 00:18:56,218
[woman sobbing distantly]

276
00:19:01,057 --> 00:19:02,224
What's that?

277
00:19:09,315 --> 00:19:11,025
[sobbing grows louder]

278
00:19:11,901 --> 00:19:13,276
[♪ jaunty music playing]

279
00:19:13,277 --> 00:19:14,445
[sobbing stops]

280
00:19:18,115 --> 00:19:21,577
TAROT MASTER
LUNA

281
00:19:27,917 --> 00:19:29,001
[electricity crackling]

282
00:19:30,169 --> 00:19:31,879
[electricity crackling]

283
00:19:34,674 --> 00:19:35,757
[♪ music fades]

284
00:19:35,758 --> 00:19:38,803
So you do tarot readings here?

285
00:19:40,805 --> 00:19:42,138
Yes.

286
00:19:42,139 --> 00:19:44,892
I do readings for people
who win the giveaway.

287
00:19:46,352 --> 00:19:47,977
[♪ soft, suspenseful music playing]

288
00:19:47,978 --> 00:19:49,063
PARK JAEHA'S MAGIC FIRE

289
00:19:49,814 --> 00:19:51,816
Were you close with Park Jaeha?

290
00:19:54,902 --> 00:19:57,237
I told him to be careful.

291
00:19:57,238 --> 00:19:59,490
You mean you knew he was going to die?

292
00:20:00,324 --> 00:20:01,325
Yes.

293
00:20:03,327 --> 00:20:05,454
I had a dream.

294
00:20:06,163 --> 00:20:08,040
Ah. [chuckles softly] A dream?

295
00:20:08,833 --> 00:20:10,251
Like a prophetic dream?

296
00:20:10,918 --> 00:20:12,127
Yes.

297
00:20:12,128 --> 00:20:15,130
I've always had a kind of sixth sense
since I was little.

298
00:20:15,131 --> 00:20:18,925
I have prophetic dreams
before something happens.

299
00:20:18,926 --> 00:20:21,136
I even knew before my grandfather died.

300
00:20:21,137 --> 00:20:22,346
Oh...

301
00:20:23,222 --> 00:20:25,015
[Luna] But yesterday,

302
00:20:25,641 --> 00:20:26,642
I saw it.

303
00:20:28,436 --> 00:20:30,396
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

304
00:20:54,420 --> 00:20:57,338
So this morning, I told him to be careful,
and he said...

305
00:20:57,339 --> 00:20:58,340
He said?

306
00:21:00,509 --> 00:21:02,678
I have to treat it
like my last performance

307
00:21:03,554 --> 00:21:04,722
and do my best.

308
00:21:05,806 --> 00:21:06,890
Jaeha.

309
00:21:06,891 --> 00:21:08,267
Thanks, Luna.

310
00:21:12,480 --> 00:21:13,773
[♪ music fades]

311
00:21:15,858 --> 00:21:18,235
Did you see anything else in that dream?

312
00:21:22,531 --> 00:21:23,615
No.

313
00:21:23,616 --> 00:21:24,784
Oh...

314
00:21:26,202 --> 00:21:28,287
All right, thank you for your cooperation.

315
00:21:30,873 --> 00:21:33,541
Wow, that's incredible.

316
00:21:33,542 --> 00:21:35,001
She had a prophetic dream.

317
00:21:35,002 --> 00:21:36,253
[exhales softly in awe]

318
00:21:36,921 --> 00:21:39,088
You don't believe that stuff, do you?

319
00:21:39,089 --> 00:21:40,173
Of course not.

320
00:21:40,174 --> 00:21:41,299
[sighs]

321
00:21:41,300 --> 00:21:43,802
When I was learning at the police academy,

322
00:21:43,803 --> 00:21:47,473
a certain instructor said,
"Accept new information without bias."

323
00:21:50,226 --> 00:21:51,643
You must've forgotten.

324
00:21:51,644 --> 00:21:54,604
When you're investigating a case,
psychics call all the time,

325
00:21:54,605 --> 00:21:56,231
claiming they know something.

326
00:21:56,232 --> 00:21:58,942
But when you ask who did it,
they suddenly can't see it.

327
00:21:58,943 --> 00:21:59,985
[scoffs softly]

328
00:22:00,528 --> 00:22:02,988
More importantly,
what Park Jaeha said is bothering me.

329
00:22:03,948 --> 00:22:05,031
What do you mean?

330
00:22:05,032 --> 00:22:07,368
He said he had to treat it
like his last performance.

331
00:22:08,369 --> 00:22:10,245
As if he knew he would die.

332
00:22:10,246 --> 00:22:11,747
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

333
00:22:12,873 --> 00:22:15,125
I have to treat it
like my last performance

334
00:22:15,876 --> 00:22:17,378
and do my best.

335
00:22:20,297 --> 00:22:21,465
Let's go to the workshop.

336
00:22:22,424 --> 00:22:23,675
Okay.

337
00:22:23,676 --> 00:22:24,802
[♪ music fades]

338
00:22:26,345 --> 00:22:28,054
I assume you haven't found much.

339
00:22:28,055 --> 00:22:29,974
Well, everything burned to a crisp.

340
00:22:30,641 --> 00:22:32,517
We'll check right away and let you know.

341
00:22:32,518 --> 00:22:33,852
- Okay.
- Good luck.

342
00:22:33,853 --> 00:22:35,187
- [Junyoung] Okay.
- [Kyungjin] Thank you, sir.

343
00:22:38,691 --> 00:22:39,733
[Junyoung sighs]

344
00:22:41,318 --> 00:22:42,486
What happened here?

345
00:22:43,571 --> 00:22:44,654
And you are?

346
00:22:44,655 --> 00:22:46,322
I'm the CEO of the production company.

347
00:22:46,323 --> 00:22:47,407
SHOW PRODUCER
CHOI MIHEE

348
00:22:47,408 --> 00:22:48,616
Did Jaeha die?

349
00:22:48,617 --> 00:22:51,245
Yes, he is deceased.

350
00:22:52,538 --> 00:22:53,621
How?

351
00:22:53,622 --> 00:22:56,959
It seems there was a problem
with the magic equipment.

352
00:22:57,960 --> 00:23:00,754
That's impossible. [scoffs in disbelief]

353
00:23:14,852 --> 00:23:15,936
[Isoo] Hello?

354
00:23:19,940 --> 00:23:20,941
[door unlocks]

355
00:23:24,695 --> 00:23:25,988
[low, mechanical whirring]

356
00:23:26,989 --> 00:23:28,949
[♪ soft, suspenseful music playing]

357
00:23:33,162 --> 00:23:34,413
Mr. Park Jaeha?

358
00:23:36,165 --> 00:23:37,957
MAGIC SHOW ENGINEER
PARK JAEHYUNG

359
00:23:37,958 --> 00:23:39,293
I'm Park Jaehyung.

360
00:23:40,085 --> 00:23:41,211
Jaeha's brother.

361
00:23:41,795 --> 00:23:43,422
You're twins.

362
00:23:46,800 --> 00:23:48,093
[Isoo exhales softly]

363
00:23:49,303 --> 00:23:50,471
We're with the police.

364
00:23:51,138 --> 00:23:52,181
[breath trembles]

365
00:23:52,848 --> 00:23:54,808
Did you hear the news?

366
00:23:55,434 --> 00:23:56,435
Yes.

367
00:23:57,394 --> 00:23:58,896
I heard it just now.

368
00:24:00,940 --> 00:24:02,649
Is it true?

369
00:24:02,650 --> 00:24:04,067
Yes.

370
00:24:04,068 --> 00:24:05,903
[♪ melancholy music playing]

371
00:24:07,905 --> 00:24:09,156
[chokes, sobs]

372
00:24:14,411 --> 00:24:15,913
[sobbing softly]

373
00:24:27,216 --> 00:24:28,342
[♪ music fades]

374
00:24:29,551 --> 00:24:32,178
We heard you build the equipment yourself.

375
00:24:32,179 --> 00:24:34,640
We used to perform together in the past,

376
00:24:36,976 --> 00:24:38,435
but after I injured my legs,

377
00:24:39,228 --> 00:24:40,562
I became an engineer.

378
00:24:42,439 --> 00:24:45,943
The performance you did together
must have been a teleportation act.

379
00:24:46,568 --> 00:24:47,569
That's right.

380
00:24:48,195 --> 00:24:49,571
Teleportation?

381
00:24:51,281 --> 00:24:52,616
We went to see a show,

382
00:24:53,325 --> 00:24:54,952
and the CEO scouted us.

383
00:24:59,123 --> 00:25:00,581
Because we're twins.

384
00:25:00,582 --> 00:25:02,084
[♪ intriguing music playing]

385
00:25:04,128 --> 00:25:06,046
[chain clinking, rattling]

386
00:25:17,558 --> 00:25:19,518
[♪ music swells]

387
00:25:22,104 --> 00:25:23,564
[audience gasps]

388
00:25:29,695 --> 00:25:32,030
[announcer] <i>Park Jaeha's Teleportation!</i>

389
00:25:32,031 --> 00:25:33,239
[audience gasps]

390
00:25:33,240 --> 00:25:34,825
[audience cheering, applauding]

391
00:25:40,497 --> 00:25:41,623
- [♪ music fades]
- [Isoo] <i>That was</i>

392
00:25:42,666 --> 00:25:44,543
done by twins?

393
00:25:45,252 --> 00:25:46,253
Yes.

394
00:25:48,881 --> 00:25:50,340
Jaeha was talented.

395
00:25:51,050 --> 00:25:52,592
[♪ soft, melancholy music playing]

396
00:25:52,593 --> 00:25:54,678
So he made his professional debut,

397
00:25:56,138 --> 00:25:58,432
and I only joined him
for the teleportation act.

398
00:26:01,810 --> 00:26:04,480
What exactly happened?

399
00:26:05,773 --> 00:26:07,273
The casket caught on fire...

400
00:26:07,274 --> 00:26:08,566
[breath trembles]

401
00:26:08,567 --> 00:26:11,319
...and your brother wasn't able to escape.

402
00:26:11,320 --> 00:26:12,446
[chokes back a sob]

403
00:26:14,865 --> 00:26:15,908
[crying softly]

404
00:26:17,034 --> 00:26:19,578
[voice shaking] I kept telling him
it was dangerous.

405
00:26:21,580 --> 00:26:23,664
Are you saying the casket was dangerous?

406
00:26:23,665 --> 00:26:25,584
If the fuel leaked,

407
00:26:27,419 --> 00:26:30,839
it could cause an accident,
so I told him not to do it.

408
00:26:32,382 --> 00:26:34,259
Then why did he...

409
00:26:35,761 --> 00:26:37,929
Jaeha always said the same thing.

410
00:26:37,930 --> 00:26:40,348
Don't you know how lucky I am, Jaehyung?

411
00:26:40,349 --> 00:26:41,933
Things like that don't happen to me.

412
00:26:41,934 --> 00:26:43,018
Okay.

413
00:26:45,020 --> 00:26:47,022
It was the same
when the accident happened.

414
00:26:48,273 --> 00:26:49,733
Jaeha was fine,

415
00:26:53,445 --> 00:26:54,780
while I ended up like this.

416
00:26:55,572 --> 00:26:57,073
So I, too,

417
00:26:57,074 --> 00:26:59,660
believed that luck was on his side,

418
00:27:01,662 --> 00:27:03,122
but then this happened. [sobbing]

419
00:27:05,207 --> 00:27:06,792
[sniffles, continues sobbing]

420
00:27:08,502 --> 00:27:09,752
[♪ music fades]

421
00:27:09,753 --> 00:27:12,296
There's no way there was
a problem with the equipment.

422
00:27:12,297 --> 00:27:14,423
Do you know how much
we rehearse before the show?

423
00:27:14,424 --> 00:27:17,135
We run it dozens, even hundreds of times
without a problem

424
00:27:17,136 --> 00:27:18,636
before it goes on stage.

425
00:27:18,637 --> 00:27:20,139
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

426
00:27:24,226 --> 00:27:25,644
[siren wailing]

427
00:27:28,939 --> 00:27:30,189
[♪ music fades]

428
00:27:30,190 --> 00:27:32,985
The production company's CEO
insists there wasn't a problem.

429
00:27:33,944 --> 00:27:36,445
She wouldn't want to admit
that it was an accident.

430
00:27:36,446 --> 00:27:37,989
The engineer said it was dangerous.

431
00:27:37,990 --> 00:27:40,116
Hey, the engineer is the magician's twin.

432
00:27:40,117 --> 00:27:41,577
- His twin?
- [Isoo] Yeah.

433
00:27:42,536 --> 00:27:43,744
[sighs heavily]

434
00:27:43,745 --> 00:27:46,206
To think the teleportation magic
was a trick with twins.

435
00:27:46,790 --> 00:27:49,126
Obviously. Did you think
he was actually teleporting?

436
00:27:49,668 --> 00:27:51,128
Do superpowers really not exist?

437
00:27:52,838 --> 00:27:54,463
Let's go back for now.

438
00:27:54,464 --> 00:27:56,883
We'll know once
the forensic results are out.

439
00:27:56,884 --> 00:27:58,760
- Okay.
- Have a good evening.

440
00:28:02,097 --> 00:28:03,265
Mr. Innocent.

441
00:28:03,932 --> 00:28:05,642
[chuckles softly] Let's go.

442
00:28:11,231 --> 00:28:13,941
So, which do you think it is?

443
00:28:13,942 --> 00:28:16,862
I can't say for sure yet. [sighs]

444
00:28:17,738 --> 00:28:19,197
But there is something strange.

445
00:28:19,781 --> 00:28:20,865
Like what?

446
00:28:20,866 --> 00:28:22,701
If this was indeed a murder,

447
00:28:23,452 --> 00:28:25,369
why was he killed on stage?

448
00:28:25,370 --> 00:28:30,249
Why create countless witnesses
by killing him during a performance?

449
00:28:30,250 --> 00:28:34,128
If a magician dies during a performance,
it can be made to look like an accident.

450
00:28:34,129 --> 00:28:37,757
But once it's revealed to be a murder,
that narrows down the suspects.

451
00:28:37,758 --> 00:28:40,510
Only a limited number of people
have access to the equipment.

452
00:28:41,637 --> 00:28:43,554
Hmm. That's true.

453
00:28:43,555 --> 00:28:44,889
[cell phone ringing over car audio]

454
00:28:44,890 --> 00:28:45,973
Sorry, one second.

455
00:28:45,974 --> 00:28:47,476
YU SEONGWON
INCOMING CALL

456
00:28:48,310 --> 00:28:51,312
Hey, Sculptor Yu.
Did the exhibition wrap up okay?

457
00:28:51,313 --> 00:28:53,898
Yeah, it just finished,
so we're packing up now.

458
00:28:53,899 --> 00:28:56,443
[Isoo] <i>Hey, did you sell all your pieces?
I wanted to buy one.</i>

459
00:28:57,152 --> 00:28:58,694
I don't sell my pieces.

460
00:28:58,695 --> 00:28:59,987
I keep them all.

461
00:28:59,988 --> 00:29:02,657
[Isoo] Oh. Well, look at you, Mr. Artist.

462
00:29:02,658 --> 00:29:05,034
I guess you don't need the money.

463
00:29:05,035 --> 00:29:06,036
Isoo.

464
00:29:06,703 --> 00:29:08,412
Let's meet up soon.

465
00:29:08,413 --> 00:29:10,414
It's been a while since I was last here.

466
00:29:10,415 --> 00:29:12,458
Yeah, we should. How long are you staying?

467
00:29:12,459 --> 00:29:16,253
<i>I have another exhibition coming up,
so I'll probably be in Korea for a while.</i>

468
00:29:16,254 --> 00:29:19,632
Got it. Then let's meet up next week.
I'll call you.

469
00:29:19,633 --> 00:29:20,883
<i>Okay, bye.</i>

470
00:29:20,884 --> 00:29:22,010
[line disconnects]

471
00:29:22,761 --> 00:29:24,054
That reminds me,

472
00:29:24,972 --> 00:29:26,138
you were at the exhibition.

473
00:29:26,139 --> 00:29:27,891
Just look at all this.

474
00:29:31,061 --> 00:29:33,729
Isoo, come this way.
You need to see this piece first.

475
00:29:33,730 --> 00:29:35,148
What? Which one?

476
00:29:36,400 --> 00:29:37,609
Yes, I was there.

477
00:29:38,652 --> 00:29:40,153
Do you like Yu Seongwon?

478
00:29:40,988 --> 00:29:42,780
I'm very interested in him.

479
00:29:42,781 --> 00:29:45,533
No wonder. You had
photos of his exhibition at home.

480
00:29:45,534 --> 00:29:47,285
I'm close with Seongwon.

481
00:29:48,996 --> 00:29:50,162
How do you know him?

482
00:29:50,163 --> 00:29:51,831
Uh...

483
00:29:51,832 --> 00:29:54,625
You know his family owns UBS Group, right?

484
00:29:54,626 --> 00:29:57,211
I met him at a gathering
for third-generation chaebol heirs.

485
00:29:57,212 --> 00:29:59,922
I haven't seen him much
since he moved to the UK,

486
00:29:59,923 --> 00:30:02,091
but he's completely fallen for my charms.

487
00:30:02,092 --> 00:30:03,592
He likes me so much.

488
00:30:03,593 --> 00:30:04,720
[Isoo exclaims smugly]

489
00:30:06,013 --> 00:30:08,890
If you want to meet him,
I can arrange something.

490
00:30:10,142 --> 00:30:11,143
Next time.

491
00:30:12,644 --> 00:30:13,729
Are you feeling shy?

492
00:30:16,231 --> 00:30:18,150
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

493
00:30:50,390 --> 00:30:52,933
SEWON HOSPITAL

494
00:30:52,934 --> 00:30:55,352
[medical monitor beeping steadily]

495
00:30:55,353 --> 00:30:57,189
[♪ soft, melancholy music playing]

496
00:30:59,691 --> 00:31:02,985
[Dr. Jinkyung] Mr. Choi Jeonghun,
we will now begin the surgery.

497
00:31:02,986 --> 00:31:04,070
All right.

498
00:31:04,071 --> 00:31:06,490
Don't worry. It's going to go well.

499
00:31:07,115 --> 00:31:09,659
Just get some sleep,
and you'll wake up healthier.

500
00:31:10,702 --> 00:31:11,786
Okay.

501
00:31:11,787 --> 00:31:13,288
We're going to put you under now.

502
00:31:14,039 --> 00:31:16,333
[anesthesiologist] We'll begin
the anesthesia now.

503
00:31:18,293 --> 00:31:21,337
[Dr. Jinkyung] Please count slowly
from one to ten.

504
00:31:21,338 --> 00:31:23,381
[Mr. Choi, muffled] One.

505
00:31:24,382 --> 00:31:25,967
Two.

506
00:31:27,511 --> 00:31:28,720
Three.

507
00:31:30,889 --> 00:31:32,056
[♪ music fades]

508
00:31:32,057 --> 00:31:35,018
SEOUL GANGHA POLICE STATION

509
00:31:36,311 --> 00:31:39,397
[Taegyun] "The magician
who burned on stage"?

510
00:31:39,940 --> 00:31:41,066
Good grief.

511
00:31:42,651 --> 00:31:46,278
Why did we end up
with another bothersome case?

512
00:31:46,279 --> 00:31:48,073
Well...

513
00:31:48,782 --> 00:31:51,242
Team 1 happened to be on site at the time.

514
00:31:51,243 --> 00:31:52,285
"Happened to be"?

515
00:31:53,453 --> 00:31:54,912
Well... [chuckles nervously]

516
00:31:54,913 --> 00:31:57,456
Detective Jin had tickets,
so they went to see the show.

517
00:31:57,457 --> 00:31:58,999
For heaven's sake.

518
00:31:59,000 --> 00:32:00,835
What's wrong with him?

519
00:32:00,836 --> 00:32:02,753
Is he a crime magnet? Jesus Christ.

520
00:32:02,754 --> 00:32:04,381
Everywhere he goes, it's a new case.

521
00:32:05,257 --> 00:32:06,340
[knock at door]

522
00:32:06,341 --> 00:32:07,425
[Taegyun] Come in.

523
00:32:08,385 --> 00:32:10,178
Right, yes. Put that in the car.

524
00:32:11,763 --> 00:32:12,848
[sighs in exasperation]

525
00:32:13,557 --> 00:32:15,975
In any case, catch the culprit quickly.

526
00:32:15,976 --> 00:32:17,518
- Got it?
- Yes, sir.

527
00:32:17,519 --> 00:32:18,770
- Yes, sir.
- [Taegyun] Right.

528
00:32:24,192 --> 00:32:25,943
PARK JAEHA, AGE 32
RENOWNED MAGICIAN

529
00:32:25,944 --> 00:32:27,820
FOUND DEAD IN A FIRE DURING A PERFORMANCE

530
00:32:27,821 --> 00:32:29,363
ACCIDENT? OR EQUIPMENT ERROR?

531
00:32:29,364 --> 00:32:31,240
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

532
00:32:31,241 --> 00:32:33,160
FIRE BREAKS OUT DURING A FIRE ESCAPE ACT

533
00:32:38,456 --> 00:32:39,499
[inhales sharply]

534
00:32:41,751 --> 00:32:44,212
This isn't an accident.
It's a murder case.

535
00:32:45,922 --> 00:32:47,883
Kerosene was detected on the casket panel.

536
00:32:52,846 --> 00:32:54,805
They normally use a special kind of oil,

537
00:32:54,806 --> 00:32:57,808
but someone poured kerosene in it,
so the flames spread inside.

538
00:32:57,809 --> 00:32:59,810
TRACES OF KEROSENE DETECTED

539
00:32:59,811 --> 00:33:02,772
Oh, and this is
the forensic analysis of his phone.

540
00:33:05,108 --> 00:33:06,151
[Junyoung scoffs softly]

541
00:33:06,735 --> 00:33:08,736
[sighs] Park Jaeha was something else.

542
00:33:08,737 --> 00:33:10,447
[scoffs] What's wrong this guy?

543
00:33:11,573 --> 00:33:12,616
Look at this.

544
00:33:15,202 --> 00:33:17,703
Let's go. They're holding
a memorial for him today.

545
00:33:17,704 --> 00:33:19,122
Okay.

546
00:33:19,831 --> 00:33:20,998
Come on.

547
00:33:20,999 --> 00:33:22,125
Let's go.

548
00:33:23,418 --> 00:33:26,378
IN MEMORY OF PARK JAEHA,
WHO GAVE US SO MANY MAGICAL MOMENTS

549
00:33:26,379 --> 00:33:29,674
THE FLAMES YOU LEFT BEHIND
STILL LIVE ON IN ALL OF US

550
00:33:30,508 --> 00:33:34,846
WE WILL FOREVER REMEMBER THE SMILE
THAT MADE US BELIEVE IN MAGIC

551
00:33:35,472 --> 00:33:37,681
THE LATE PARK JAEHA (1992-2025)

552
00:33:37,682 --> 00:33:39,642
[♪ somber, melancholy music playing]

553
00:33:39,643 --> 00:33:41,269
[camera shutters clicking]

554
00:33:42,854 --> 00:33:45,315
Let us have a moment of silence.

555
00:33:52,072 --> 00:33:54,031
WE WON'T FORGET THE MIRACLES YOU CREATED

556
00:33:54,032 --> 00:33:55,825
MAY YOU REST IN PEACE, JAEHA

557
00:33:59,037 --> 00:34:00,038
Thank you.

558
00:34:06,294 --> 00:34:07,379
[sniffles]

559
00:34:08,505 --> 00:34:09,838
[sighs softly]

560
00:34:09,839 --> 00:34:10,966
[♪ music fades]

561
00:34:11,841 --> 00:34:15,761
The fans wanted to pay their respects,
so we arranged this memorial.

562
00:34:15,762 --> 00:34:18,722
When can we hold the funeral?

563
00:34:18,723 --> 00:34:20,642
I think this is going to take some time.

564
00:34:22,477 --> 00:34:24,354
We believe someone murdered Mr. Park.

565
00:34:26,564 --> 00:34:29,400
Do you know anyone
who might want him dead?

566
00:34:29,401 --> 00:34:30,985
[Mihee] No, not at all.

567
00:34:30,986 --> 00:34:33,028
Jaeha was always so cheerful and kind.

568
00:34:33,029 --> 00:34:35,031
He wasn't the kind of person
anyone would hate.

569
00:34:45,667 --> 00:34:48,169
[sobbing] How could something
like this happen?

570
00:34:48,962 --> 00:34:50,672
This is just so horrible.

571
00:34:55,135 --> 00:34:56,511
[continues sobbing]

572
00:35:00,390 --> 00:35:01,849
The truth is,

573
00:35:01,850 --> 00:35:04,728
I was in a relationship with him.

574
00:35:05,937 --> 00:35:07,230
[♪ jaunty music playing]

575
00:35:09,190 --> 00:35:10,525
What are you talking about?

576
00:35:12,902 --> 00:35:14,486
It's been 50 days.

577
00:35:14,487 --> 00:35:15,613
[scoffs]

578
00:35:15,614 --> 00:35:17,156
I've dated him for over a year.

579
00:35:17,157 --> 00:35:18,657
I'm sure you just had a crush.

580
00:35:18,658 --> 00:35:21,161
You dated him?
Are you sure you didn't imagine it?

581
00:35:25,498 --> 00:35:27,041
Jaeha bought this for me.

582
00:35:27,042 --> 00:35:28,585
- [scoffs] Me too.
- Me too.

583
00:35:32,047 --> 00:35:33,340
[Jiyun] He bought it for you?

584
00:35:34,341 --> 00:35:35,383
No way.

585
00:35:36,259 --> 00:35:37,761
I'm sure it was as a thank-you.

586
00:35:38,928 --> 00:35:40,554
You're the one who's delusional.

587
00:35:40,555 --> 00:35:42,640
Jaeha has really high standards.

588
00:35:42,641 --> 00:35:44,683
Yeah, you're way older than him, too.

589
00:35:44,684 --> 00:35:46,852
What does age have to do with anything?

590
00:35:46,853 --> 00:35:48,729
He called you immature and tacky.

591
00:35:48,730 --> 00:35:49,897
[scoffs]

592
00:35:49,898 --> 00:35:51,357
You mean "pure and innocent."

593
00:35:51,358 --> 00:35:53,984
He said he discovered true love
only after meeting me.

594
00:35:53,985 --> 00:35:55,861
[scoffs] We kept it a secret,

595
00:35:55,862 --> 00:35:59,323
but we were going to get married
next year.

596
00:35:59,324 --> 00:36:02,451
We were looking
for a place to move in together

597
00:36:02,452 --> 00:36:04,746
- and register our marriage next month.
- Marriage?

598
00:36:07,540 --> 00:36:08,916
[sighs deeply]

599
00:36:08,917 --> 00:36:10,584
There's no way.

600
00:36:10,585 --> 00:36:12,628
Why would he be into you two?

601
00:36:12,629 --> 00:36:14,838
What? Watch what you say.

602
00:36:14,839 --> 00:36:16,173
You watch what you say.

603
00:36:16,174 --> 00:36:18,509
Don't say whatever you want
just because he's dead!

604
00:36:18,510 --> 00:36:20,553
- Hey!
- [Dahee] Move in together? As if.

605
00:36:21,721 --> 00:36:24,390
I'm the one Jaeha truly loved.

606
00:36:24,391 --> 00:36:26,058
It's neither of you.

607
00:36:26,059 --> 00:36:28,185
I'm the one he chose in the end.

608
00:36:28,186 --> 00:36:30,980
He told me you stalked him.

609
00:36:31,856 --> 00:36:33,565
How dare you! Come here.

610
00:36:33,566 --> 00:36:36,443
[Isoo] Wait, hold on. Break it up.

611
00:36:36,444 --> 00:36:38,112
Violence is wrong.

612
00:36:38,113 --> 00:36:39,196
[Dahee] What do you want?

613
00:36:39,197 --> 00:36:41,532
We're in the middle
of something important.

614
00:36:41,533 --> 00:36:43,742
I know. It sounds pretty serious.

615
00:36:43,743 --> 00:36:46,495
But that something important is
pointless now.

616
00:36:46,496 --> 00:36:48,790
I checked Mr. Park Jaeha's phone records.

617
00:36:49,749 --> 00:36:50,875
Uh...

618
00:36:52,585 --> 00:36:54,128
- Jiyun?
- Yes.

619
00:36:54,129 --> 00:36:56,880
- You're "Honey 1."
- What?

620
00:36:56,881 --> 00:36:58,382
- And Dahee.
- Yes?

621
00:36:58,383 --> 00:37:00,468
- You're "Honey 2."
- What?

622
00:37:01,177 --> 00:37:02,261
- Luna?
- Yes?

623
00:37:02,262 --> 00:37:03,763
You're "Honey 6."

624
00:37:05,014 --> 00:37:06,015
Six?

625
00:37:08,309 --> 00:37:10,103
What's that supposed to mean?

626
00:37:10,979 --> 00:37:13,564
It means
Mr. Park Jaeha had a lot of girlfriends.

627
00:37:13,565 --> 00:37:17,234
In other words, you were all his honeys.

628
00:37:17,235 --> 00:37:19,486
There were seven honeys in total.

629
00:37:19,487 --> 00:37:21,822
[whispering] He must have
so much love to give.

630
00:37:21,823 --> 00:37:24,199
[stuttering] Seven people?

631
00:37:24,200 --> 00:37:26,828
Didn't you always go on dates
on the same day each week?

632
00:37:27,662 --> 00:37:28,912
Seven women, seven days.

633
00:37:28,913 --> 00:37:31,166
It must be Monday, Tuesday, and Saturday.

634
00:37:33,084 --> 00:37:34,711
Hold on.

635
00:37:36,379 --> 00:37:38,964
These are all fakes.
You lent him money too, right?

636
00:37:38,965 --> 00:37:41,009
- [gasps]
- Let's talk at the station.

637
00:37:42,010 --> 00:37:44,012
- Detective Park.
- Yes.

638
00:37:45,138 --> 00:37:46,513
- [Isoo] Let's go.
- [sighs]

639
00:37:46,514 --> 00:37:48,182
- [Junyoung] Come on.
- Just for some small talk.

640
00:37:48,183 --> 00:37:50,559
It's part of the investigation.
Come on, honeys.

641
00:37:50,560 --> 00:37:52,437
Let's talk at the station.

642
00:37:56,524 --> 00:37:57,901
[♪ music fades]

643
00:38:00,779 --> 00:38:01,863
Murder?

644
00:38:03,156 --> 00:38:04,157
You mean...

645
00:38:05,116 --> 00:38:07,202
someone killed Jaeha?

646
00:38:07,827 --> 00:38:08,828
Yes.

647
00:38:09,621 --> 00:38:12,873
Someone poured kerosene inside the casket.

648
00:38:12,874 --> 00:38:13,875
Who?

649
00:38:15,043 --> 00:38:18,588
Do you know if there was anyone
who wanted to kill your brother?

650
00:38:21,466 --> 00:38:23,593
If anyone comes to mind, please tell us.

651
00:38:25,512 --> 00:38:26,513
No.

652
00:38:27,305 --> 00:38:29,474
Jaeha was the type of person

653
00:38:30,558 --> 00:38:32,185
who was always in the spotlight.

654
00:38:32,727 --> 00:38:34,479
[♪ gentle piano music playing]

655
00:38:36,898 --> 00:38:38,316
[applauding]

656
00:38:46,366 --> 00:38:48,576
Everyone loved him.

657
00:38:49,285 --> 00:38:51,453
A little too much, I think.

658
00:38:51,454 --> 00:38:52,788
Sorry?

659
00:38:52,789 --> 00:38:56,583
We've confirmed
that Mr. Park had seven girlfriends.

660
00:38:56,584 --> 00:38:58,086
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

661
00:38:59,254 --> 00:39:00,964
He was always popular.

662
00:39:01,840 --> 00:39:04,384
It wasn't that he was popular.
He was a womanizer.

663
00:39:05,009 --> 00:39:06,678
He dated seven women at once.

664
00:39:07,595 --> 00:39:10,097
Was he in trouble at all
because of a woman?

665
00:39:10,098 --> 00:39:11,599
Did he say anything of the sort?

666
00:39:13,893 --> 00:39:14,894
No.

667
00:39:16,813 --> 00:39:17,981
[sighs softly]

668
00:39:19,274 --> 00:39:20,399
[♪ music fades]

669
00:39:20,400 --> 00:39:22,527
SEOUL GANGHA POLICE STATION

670
00:39:23,236 --> 00:39:25,947
[Dahee] He said it'd be awkward
if other people found out,

671
00:39:26,573 --> 00:39:28,407
and that we should keep it a secret.

672
00:39:28,408 --> 00:39:30,785
Workplace relationships are never easy.

673
00:39:31,703 --> 00:39:32,745
[clears throat]

674
00:39:33,830 --> 00:39:35,999
Did you really not know he was cheating?

675
00:39:37,625 --> 00:39:38,626
Uh...

676
00:39:39,878 --> 00:39:42,213
I did notice something that felt off.

677
00:39:42,714 --> 00:39:44,674
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

678
00:39:50,763 --> 00:39:52,140
[both chuckle softly]

679
00:39:59,606 --> 00:40:01,149
You're upset with me, aren't you?

680
00:40:02,317 --> 00:40:04,610
It's just weird.

681
00:40:04,611 --> 00:40:07,614
We're just good friends
because we've worked together for so long.

682
00:40:08,406 --> 00:40:09,782
I have this beautiful,

683
00:40:10,491 --> 00:40:13,411
adorable girlfriend,
so why would I look at anyone else?

684
00:40:14,954 --> 00:40:15,955
[scoffs incredulously]

685
00:40:16,789 --> 00:40:17,790
Wait.

686
00:40:18,499 --> 00:40:19,500
You're blinding me.

687
00:40:20,919 --> 00:40:21,920
[scoffs]

688
00:40:23,504 --> 00:40:25,131
When I look into your eyes,

689
00:40:26,633 --> 00:40:27,759
I see diamonds.

690
00:40:32,221 --> 00:40:33,388
[squeals]

691
00:40:33,389 --> 00:40:34,390
And it's right here.

692
00:40:36,184 --> 00:40:37,477
Oh my god!

693
00:40:39,062 --> 00:40:40,730
When did you prepare this?

694
00:40:41,397 --> 00:40:42,440
It's nothing much.

695
00:40:43,733 --> 00:40:45,025
[softly] Ah...

696
00:40:45,026 --> 00:40:46,194
[Jaeha chuckles softly]

697
00:40:46,945 --> 00:40:49,071
- [keyboard clacking]
- [♪ music fades]

698
00:40:49,072 --> 00:40:52,366
[Junyoung] "When I look into your eyes,
I see diamonds."

699
00:40:52,367 --> 00:40:56,162
So that's the kind of thing
women like to hear.

700
00:40:57,914 --> 00:40:59,499
He was really affectionate.

701
00:40:59,999 --> 00:41:01,375
[♪ gentle piano music playing]

702
00:41:01,376 --> 00:41:02,961
Your pretty hands are all beat up.

703
00:41:03,711 --> 00:41:04,795
It's fine.

704
00:41:04,796 --> 00:41:07,173
- Want me to show you my new magic trick?
- Yes.

705
00:41:14,389 --> 00:41:15,640
It's a ring.

706
00:41:16,724 --> 00:41:17,767
It's beautiful.

707
00:41:21,312 --> 00:41:22,522
[Jiyun gasps]

708
00:41:24,107 --> 00:41:25,108
Oh my god.

709
00:41:26,317 --> 00:41:27,318
That's amazing.

710
00:41:27,944 --> 00:41:29,028
[gasps softly]

711
00:41:34,033 --> 00:41:35,034
Where did it go?

712
00:41:51,300 --> 00:41:52,384
[chuckles softly]

713
00:41:52,385 --> 00:41:53,553
Will you marry me?

714
00:41:56,472 --> 00:41:57,640
[whimpers softly]

715
00:41:59,183 --> 00:42:01,685
- [patron 1] Congratulations.
- [patron 2] Way to go.

716
00:42:01,686 --> 00:42:02,769
[patron 3] Congratulations.

717
00:42:02,770 --> 00:42:04,355
[patrons cheering, applauding]

718
00:42:05,565 --> 00:42:07,191
[♪ soft, melancholy music playing]

719
00:42:09,360 --> 00:42:10,694
JAEHA "WILL YOU MARRY ME?"

720
00:42:10,695 --> 00:42:13,780
Getting down on your knees
and proposing in a public place

721
00:42:13,781 --> 00:42:15,824
is something women hate, isn't it?

722
00:42:15,825 --> 00:42:17,201
It depends on the person.

723
00:42:17,785 --> 00:42:18,995
[whispering] He's new to dating.

724
00:42:20,371 --> 00:42:21,997
But I was still number one,

725
00:42:21,998 --> 00:42:24,041
so he must have liked me best, right?

726
00:42:24,042 --> 00:42:26,793
- You were just the longest.
- [keyboard clacking]

727
00:42:26,794 --> 00:42:28,336
[♪ jaunty music playing]

728
00:42:28,337 --> 00:42:29,838
[sighs in exasperation]

729
00:42:29,839 --> 00:42:32,050
I thought it was destiny.

730
00:42:32,842 --> 00:42:34,218
Pick a card.

731
00:42:38,598 --> 00:42:39,973
[both gasp softly]

732
00:42:39,974 --> 00:42:41,225
Once more.

733
00:42:43,311 --> 00:42:45,480
[Jaeha hums drumroll, chuckles]

734
00:42:47,648 --> 00:42:49,107
[both] Oh!

735
00:42:49,108 --> 00:42:50,693
- What on earth?
- One last time.

736
00:42:53,654 --> 00:42:54,738
[Jaeha] Oh!

737
00:42:54,739 --> 00:42:55,907
How did you do it?

738
00:42:56,866 --> 00:42:58,158
[Jaeha chuckles]

739
00:42:58,159 --> 00:42:59,701
I didn't do anything.

740
00:42:59,702 --> 00:43:01,329
I told you, it's destiny.

741
00:43:02,872 --> 00:43:04,081
Oh, you.

742
00:43:04,082 --> 00:43:06,666
Why did he say he needed to borrow money?

743
00:43:06,667 --> 00:43:08,710
He said he needed it for his brother.

744
00:43:08,711 --> 00:43:09,920
For a car accident.

745
00:43:09,921 --> 00:43:11,254
To get a place to live.

746
00:43:11,255 --> 00:43:13,216
He said he'd pay it back quickly.

747
00:43:13,800 --> 00:43:15,468
- [exhales deeply]
- [sighs thoughtfully]

748
00:43:17,095 --> 00:43:18,304
[♪ music fades]

749
00:43:19,305 --> 00:43:20,515
How much did you lend him?

750
00:43:22,016 --> 00:43:23,767
- Two hundred thousand?
- Two million won.

751
00:43:23,768 --> 00:43:25,644
- Are you crazy?
- [sighs softly]

752
00:43:25,645 --> 00:43:27,270
I even cashed out my savings.

753
00:43:27,271 --> 00:43:28,981
DETECTIVE DIVISION

754
00:43:34,070 --> 00:43:35,780
[♪ jaunty, dramatic music playing]

755
00:43:40,993 --> 00:43:43,121
NATIONAL POLICE AGENCY

756
00:43:53,589 --> 00:43:55,424
Let's go have some soju.

757
00:43:56,509 --> 00:43:59,302
And think about
how to exhume and desecrate him.

758
00:43:59,303 --> 00:44:01,347
What does that mean?

759
00:44:03,099 --> 00:44:05,768
It means taking him out of the grave
and killing him again.

760
00:44:10,481 --> 00:44:11,566
[♪ music fades]

761
00:44:12,608 --> 00:44:13,985
Even so,

762
00:44:15,153 --> 00:44:18,573
would they have killed him for cheating?

763
00:44:19,448 --> 00:44:21,575
He was cheating on seven people.

764
00:44:21,576 --> 00:44:23,869
Any one of them
could've been angry enough.

765
00:44:23,870 --> 00:44:24,912
Oh.

766
00:44:26,330 --> 00:44:27,957
They won't have known.

767
00:44:30,001 --> 00:44:32,003
Jaeha can be quite meticulous.

768
00:44:32,670 --> 00:44:35,005
Then who could it be?

769
00:44:35,006 --> 00:44:37,091
[♪ suspenseful, melancholy music playing]

770
00:44:39,510 --> 00:44:40,511
[voice shaking] I honestly...

771
00:44:43,347 --> 00:44:44,557
have no idea.

772
00:44:46,517 --> 00:44:48,311
I know him best.

773
00:44:48,936 --> 00:44:51,063
He's not the type of person
anyone would hate.

774
00:44:52,440 --> 00:44:53,733
Who in the world...

775
00:44:56,485 --> 00:44:58,446
could have done such a horrible thing?

776
00:44:59,405 --> 00:45:00,406
I really,

777
00:45:02,158 --> 00:45:03,743
honestly don't know.

778
00:45:04,202 --> 00:45:05,327
[sobs]

779
00:45:05,328 --> 00:45:06,412
[sighs heavily]

780
00:45:07,205 --> 00:45:08,289
[thud]

781
00:45:09,707 --> 00:45:11,124
- [gasps]
- [dove cooing]

782
00:45:11,125 --> 00:45:12,585
[♪ upbeat, jaunty music playing]

783
00:45:14,712 --> 00:45:16,214
- [air hisses]
- [gasps, yelps]

784
00:45:26,307 --> 00:45:27,600
[in English] Magic show.

785
00:45:29,477 --> 00:45:31,229
[in Korean] You shouldn't touch anything.

786
00:45:32,104 --> 00:45:34,732
There's a lot of interesting things here.

787
00:45:42,823 --> 00:45:43,991
[♪ music fades]

788
00:45:49,830 --> 00:45:50,914
He's the killer.

789
00:45:50,915 --> 00:45:53,291
What? Where did that come from?

790
00:45:53,292 --> 00:45:54,794
He was about to get up just now.

791
00:45:55,544 --> 00:45:56,628
I didn't see it.

792
00:45:56,629 --> 00:45:58,713
You're not very observant for a detective.

793
00:45:58,714 --> 00:46:01,675
I was too busy being embarrassed
by your dove flying act.

794
00:46:01,676 --> 00:46:03,510
I saw it with my own two eyes.

795
00:46:03,511 --> 00:46:04,887
[♪ soft, suspenseful music playing]

796
00:46:05,346 --> 00:46:06,597
[gasps]

797
00:46:08,891 --> 00:46:10,434
Maybe his legs have healed.

798
00:46:11,102 --> 00:46:13,312
He hid that fact and killed his brother.

799
00:46:14,146 --> 00:46:15,940
- Why?
- His motive was

800
00:46:17,275 --> 00:46:18,442
jealousy.

801
00:46:19,026 --> 00:46:20,777
They're twins,

802
00:46:20,778 --> 00:46:23,738
but Jaeha lived the high life,
doing magic and cheating on women.

803
00:46:23,739 --> 00:46:26,325
Whereas he's stuck in a wheelchair.

804
00:46:28,119 --> 00:46:29,203
[sighs deeply]

805
00:46:29,996 --> 00:46:32,998
LOVER'S REVENGE?
PARK JAEHA, HONEY 1 LEE JIYUN

806
00:46:32,999 --> 00:46:34,374
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

807
00:46:34,375 --> 00:46:36,877
HONEY 2 JEONG DAHEE, HONEY 6 LUNA

808
00:46:39,171 --> 00:46:41,673
STAGE DIRECTOR,
PERFORMANCE PARTNER, TAROT MASTER

809
00:46:41,674 --> 00:46:44,176
I don't think the three of them
knew he was cheating.

810
00:46:45,261 --> 00:46:47,596
- You sure they're not acting?
- Didn't seem like it.

811
00:46:49,098 --> 00:46:51,099
- Did you check on the kerosene?
- [Kyungjin] Yes.

812
00:46:51,100 --> 00:46:53,310
I called all the gas stations
near the theater,

813
00:46:53,311 --> 00:46:55,313
but no one's bought kerosene recently.

814
00:46:56,063 --> 00:46:57,440
PARK JAEHYUNG

815
00:46:58,024 --> 00:46:59,107
What about his brother?

816
00:46:59,108 --> 00:47:01,359
He says there isn't anyone
who'd want to kill him.

817
00:47:01,360 --> 00:47:04,029
INVOLVED WITH MULTIPLE WOMEN
SIGNS OF FINANCIAL EXPLOITATION

818
00:47:04,030 --> 00:47:05,906
He also didn't know he was a cheater.

819
00:47:07,366 --> 00:47:10,452
[sighs wearily] I really think
the brother is suspicious.

820
00:47:10,453 --> 00:47:11,536
- [♪ music fades]
- What do you mean?

821
00:47:11,537 --> 00:47:13,831
I made a dove fly out earlier.

822
00:47:15,207 --> 00:47:17,167
- A dove?
- Why?

823
00:47:17,168 --> 00:47:18,460
While stumbling around.

824
00:47:18,461 --> 00:47:21,296
It's an investigative technique. Look.

825
00:47:21,297 --> 00:47:22,922
I made the dove... You do it.

826
00:47:22,923 --> 00:47:25,133
I made the dove fly out like this,

827
00:47:25,134 --> 00:47:27,678
then Mr. Park Jaehyung
suddenly flinched like this.

828
00:47:28,679 --> 00:47:29,804
[scoffs]

829
00:47:29,805 --> 00:47:31,139
[Kyungjin] Then, you mean

830
00:47:31,140 --> 00:47:32,557
he's able to walk?

831
00:47:32,558 --> 00:47:33,892
Exactly.

832
00:47:33,893 --> 00:47:35,435
No way.

833
00:47:35,436 --> 00:47:39,273
I think he's able to walk, but pretended
not to and killed his brother.

834
00:47:41,776 --> 00:47:44,236
[sighs] Do you agree with him,
Detective Joo?

835
00:47:45,613 --> 00:47:46,655
I don't know.

836
00:47:48,449 --> 00:47:50,533
Let's check the outside security footage.

837
00:47:50,534 --> 00:47:51,743
Okay.

838
00:47:51,744 --> 00:47:53,203
[♪ tense, ticking music playing]

839
00:47:53,204 --> 00:47:55,748
[inhales deeply, exhales]

840
00:47:58,667 --> 00:48:00,169
[mouse clicking]

841
00:48:08,469 --> 00:48:11,179
Ms. Lee Jiyun said
nothing was wrong with the casket, right?

842
00:48:11,180 --> 00:48:14,225
Yes, she last checked around 4:30 p.m.

843
00:48:24,235 --> 00:48:25,611
Oh, there's the casket.

844
00:48:35,746 --> 00:48:36,747
[in English] Okay.

845
00:48:37,373 --> 00:48:39,958
[in Korean] She checked the casket
at 4:30 p.m.

846
00:48:39,959 --> 00:48:41,793
The show started at 5:00 p.m.

847
00:48:41,794 --> 00:48:44,170
The fire broke out at 5:50 p.m.

848
00:48:44,171 --> 00:48:48,341
If Mr. Park Jaehyung messed with
the equipment after Ms. Lee checked it,

849
00:48:48,342 --> 00:48:51,387
he would've left the workshop
between 4:30 and 5:50 p.m.

850
00:48:55,683 --> 00:48:58,394
I heard they return the equipment
to the workshop after the show.

851
00:49:14,201 --> 00:49:18,413
Ah, when we went,
Mr. Park Jaehyung was inside the workshop.

852
00:49:18,414 --> 00:49:19,747
He never left.

853
00:49:19,748 --> 00:49:22,501
That's the only way out
for someone in a wheelchair.

854
00:49:23,669 --> 00:49:25,962
My gut tells me it's him.

855
00:49:25,963 --> 00:49:28,799
If, just like I said,

856
00:49:29,800 --> 00:49:33,011
he could walk, he can crawl
out of the window and go around.

857
00:49:33,012 --> 00:49:34,095
And avoid the cameras.

858
00:49:34,096 --> 00:49:35,431
You're obsessing again.

859
00:49:36,056 --> 00:49:37,224
My gut's telling me.

860
00:49:39,101 --> 00:49:42,479
- Let's investigate the brother too.
- See? She trusts my instincts.

861
00:49:42,480 --> 00:49:43,731
It's just to check.

862
00:49:44,273 --> 00:49:46,566
Then I'll look into him tomorrow.

863
00:49:46,567 --> 00:49:47,776
[Hyera] Okay.

864
00:49:48,694 --> 00:49:49,777
Hey.

865
00:49:49,778 --> 00:49:51,614
[♪ tense pulsating music playing]

866
00:49:53,073 --> 00:49:56,577
Could Ms. Lee Jiyun
and Mr. Park Jaehyung be accomplices?

867
00:49:58,037 --> 00:50:00,873
A betrayed woman
and a jealous brother working together.

868
00:50:03,125 --> 00:50:07,003
[♪ music fades]

869
00:50:07,004 --> 00:50:08,755
- I'm going home.
- Me too.

870
00:50:08,756 --> 00:50:10,715
Hey, I'm not done explaining my theory.

871
00:50:10,716 --> 00:50:12,133
[Hyera] You should go home, too.

872
00:50:12,134 --> 00:50:13,552
[♪ jaunty music plays]

873
00:50:17,765 --> 00:50:19,683
SEWON HOSPITAL

874
00:50:28,776 --> 00:50:29,777
[knock on door]

875
00:50:32,321 --> 00:50:34,114
- [gasps] Ah.
- [door closes]

876
00:50:36,492 --> 00:50:37,493
How are you feeling?

877
00:50:38,160 --> 00:50:40,787
I'm doing better than I thought.

878
00:50:40,788 --> 00:50:42,789
That's always the case.

879
00:50:42,790 --> 00:50:44,666
Thinking about it is the scariest part.

880
00:50:44,667 --> 00:50:47,544
Once it's over,
you realize it's not so bad after all.

881
00:50:47,545 --> 00:50:49,170
That happens quite often.

882
00:50:49,171 --> 00:50:51,048
[chuckles] You're right.

883
00:50:52,424 --> 00:50:54,509
I heard you're the chairman of a company,

884
00:50:54,510 --> 00:50:55,636
but it's been so quiet.

885
00:50:56,762 --> 00:50:58,054
Uh...

886
00:50:58,055 --> 00:51:00,599
I didn't want to bother my staff,
so I didn't tell them.

887
00:51:01,225 --> 00:51:02,684
I just took time off work.

888
00:51:02,685 --> 00:51:03,935
What about your wife?

889
00:51:03,936 --> 00:51:06,146
I'm not married.

890
00:51:06,939 --> 00:51:08,523
I never got the chance.

891
00:51:08,524 --> 00:51:09,900
That's wise of you.

892
00:51:11,068 --> 00:51:12,695
I've been there.

893
00:51:12,903 --> 00:51:14,195
[sighs regretfully]

894
00:51:14,196 --> 00:51:16,240
- [chuckling]
- Ah. [chuckles softly]

895
00:51:16,991 --> 00:51:19,534
But you must feel lonely
being by yourself at night.

896
00:51:19,535 --> 00:51:21,160
Well,

897
00:51:21,161 --> 00:51:22,870
it's nice and quiet. [chuckles]

898
00:51:22,871 --> 00:51:24,289
I understand.

899
00:51:24,290 --> 00:51:26,624
Get plenty of sleep.
That's the best medicine.

900
00:51:26,625 --> 00:51:27,917
[chuckles]

901
00:51:27,918 --> 00:51:29,586
Call for us if you're in pain.

902
00:51:29,587 --> 00:51:31,296
I will. [chuckles]

903
00:51:31,297 --> 00:51:33,257
- Go on home.
- All right.

904
00:51:33,966 --> 00:51:34,967
Bye.

905
00:51:37,136 --> 00:51:38,178
[door opens]

906
00:51:41,223 --> 00:51:42,808
- [door closes]
- [exhales in relief]

907
00:51:43,726 --> 00:51:48,271
It's 11:00 p.m. on October 12, 2023,
at Jangseon-dong.

908
00:51:48,272 --> 00:51:50,523
October 12.

909
00:51:50,524 --> 00:51:52,942
JANGSEON-DONG DUI COLLISION
INVESTIGATION REPORT

910
00:51:52,943 --> 00:51:54,694
- Seongjun.
- Yes?

911
00:51:54,695 --> 00:51:56,988
You responded to this accident, right?

912
00:51:56,989 --> 00:51:58,406
The one with the twins.

913
00:51:58,407 --> 00:52:00,283
- [Seongjun] Yes, I did.
- What happened?

914
00:52:00,284 --> 00:52:01,993
A vehicle crashed into a building.

915
00:52:01,994 --> 00:52:03,911
The driver was heavily intoxicated.

916
00:52:03,912 --> 00:52:05,663
Who was the driver?

917
00:52:05,664 --> 00:52:07,957
It was the younger of the twins.

918
00:52:07,958 --> 00:52:09,167
Mr. Park Jaeha.

919
00:52:09,168 --> 00:52:10,835
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

920
00:52:10,836 --> 00:52:12,837
It's funny how luck works.

921
00:52:12,838 --> 00:52:16,382
The drunk driver wasn't even wearing
a seatbelt, but he was completely fine,

922
00:52:16,383 --> 00:52:18,218
whereas his brother was badly hurt.

923
00:52:22,973 --> 00:52:24,349
[♪ music swells, fades]

924
00:52:24,350 --> 00:52:27,477
Mr. Park Jaehyung has
a traumatic spinal cord injury,

925
00:52:27,478 --> 00:52:28,604
so he is unable to walk.

926
00:52:29,813 --> 00:52:32,357
Is there any chance,

927
00:52:32,358 --> 00:52:33,692
even the slightest chance,

928
00:52:34,568 --> 00:52:37,528
that he could miraculously stand up
and walk again?

929
00:52:37,529 --> 00:52:38,863
Not even a tiny chance?

930
00:52:38,864 --> 00:52:41,283
If a miracle happened, he could walk.

931
00:52:42,076 --> 00:52:44,078
That's what a miracle is, isn't it?

932
00:52:45,746 --> 00:52:47,455
Right. That's true.

933
00:52:47,456 --> 00:52:49,499
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

934
00:52:49,500 --> 00:52:50,918
[sighs wearily]

935
00:52:56,048 --> 00:52:57,049
That looks suspicious.

936
00:52:57,716 --> 00:52:58,717
[Hyera] It does.

937
00:53:00,177 --> 00:53:01,929
- Check who owns the vehicle.
- Okay.

938
00:53:02,513 --> 00:53:03,763
[keyboard clacking]

939
00:53:03,764 --> 00:53:05,473
VEHICLE REGISTRATION SEARCH

940
00:53:05,474 --> 00:53:06,892
[♪ music increases in tempo]

941
00:53:10,312 --> 00:53:12,356
OWNER HAM SEONGWOOK

942
00:53:14,108 --> 00:53:15,317
Ham Seongwook.

943
00:53:17,569 --> 00:53:18,570
He did have a motive.

944
00:53:19,613 --> 00:53:22,240
Park Jaeha crashed the car
while driving drunk,

945
00:53:22,241 --> 00:53:23,742
and his brother was injured.

946
00:53:24,326 --> 00:53:25,993
[Isoo clicks tongue, inhales deeply]

947
00:53:25,994 --> 00:53:28,538
That accident left him paralyzed
from the waist down.

948
00:53:28,539 --> 00:53:30,164
Is there a chance he could walk?

949
00:53:30,165 --> 00:53:31,166
Yes.

950
00:53:33,127 --> 00:53:34,585
- If a miracle happened.
- [♪ music fades]

951
00:53:34,586 --> 00:53:35,838
Oh, come on.

952
00:53:37,297 --> 00:53:38,965
Anyway, come look at this.

953
00:53:38,966 --> 00:53:40,968
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

954
00:53:45,180 --> 00:53:46,223
[keyboard key clacks]

955
00:53:47,266 --> 00:53:49,017
[Hyera] This is three days
before the incident.

956
00:53:52,229 --> 00:53:53,312
[keyboard key clacks]

957
00:53:53,313 --> 00:53:55,357
The vehicle is owned by Ham Seongwook.

958
00:53:56,525 --> 00:53:58,818
Ham Seongwook?
You mean that Ham Seongwook?

959
00:53:58,819 --> 00:53:59,820
Yes.

960
00:54:00,863 --> 00:54:02,030
I thought he retired.

961
00:54:03,031 --> 00:54:05,451
I thought so too, but maybe not.

962
00:54:06,535 --> 00:54:07,827
Who's Ham Seongwook?

963
00:54:07,828 --> 00:54:10,664
He's the boss of Hammurabi,
the biggest crime syndicate in Seoul.

964
00:54:11,415 --> 00:54:12,999
[victim whimpers, mutters]

965
00:54:13,000 --> 00:54:14,751
[yelping in terror]

966
00:54:14,752 --> 00:54:16,462
[breathing frantically]

967
00:54:18,005 --> 00:54:21,507
FORMER BOSS OF HAMMURABI CLAN
HAM SEONGWOOK

968
00:54:21,508 --> 00:54:23,093
[♪ music increases in tempo]

969
00:54:26,305 --> 00:54:27,555
- [blunt thud]
- [victim exclaims]

970
00:54:27,556 --> 00:54:28,639
[♪ music fades]

971
00:54:28,640 --> 00:54:32,310
He got 12 years for soliciting murder,
and he's been quiet since he got out.

972
00:54:32,311 --> 00:54:34,353
What would a gangster want
with a magician?

973
00:54:34,354 --> 00:54:36,231
We'll have to find out.

974
00:54:39,902 --> 00:54:41,319
Oh!

975
00:54:41,320 --> 00:54:44,864
There were some guys who looked like
thugs sitting behind us at the theater.

976
00:54:44,865 --> 00:54:46,575
[♪ tense pulsating music playing]

977
00:54:48,118 --> 00:54:50,077
[whispering] Please stop
kicking my seat, okay?

978
00:54:50,078 --> 00:54:51,622
[softly] Are your legs too long?

979
00:54:52,956 --> 00:54:54,082
Yeah, you're right.

980
00:54:55,042 --> 00:54:57,169
They were there
on the day of the incident.

981
00:54:58,170 --> 00:54:59,171
[keyboard clacks]

982
00:55:01,381 --> 00:55:02,424
[keyboard key clacks]

983
00:55:03,091 --> 00:55:06,677
Let's find out where Ham Seongwook is
and also identify those thugs.

984
00:55:06,678 --> 00:55:08,138
- Got it.
- [Kyungjin] Got it.

985
00:55:08,764 --> 00:55:10,973
- Do you remember their faces?
- Of course.

986
00:55:10,974 --> 00:55:12,518
They had terrible manners.

987
00:55:13,894 --> 00:55:15,102
[♪ music fades]

988
00:55:15,103 --> 00:55:18,023
[Isoo sighs] Look at these faces.
They look mean as hell.

989
00:55:19,066 --> 00:55:21,567
You really can tell a lot from a face.

990
00:55:21,568 --> 00:55:22,777
Any idea who they are?

991
00:55:22,778 --> 00:55:24,780
Mmm-mmm. Not in the slightest.

992
00:55:25,906 --> 00:55:27,115
Look at them.

993
00:55:28,325 --> 00:55:30,744
They all look the same. [sighs softly]

994
00:55:33,163 --> 00:55:34,580
Detective Joo!

995
00:55:34,581 --> 00:55:37,124
I found out how Ham Seongwook
and Park Jaeha know each other.

996
00:55:37,125 --> 00:55:38,709
[♪ suspenseful, ticking music playing]

997
00:55:38,710 --> 00:55:39,753
Here.

998
00:55:40,837 --> 00:55:42,172
[Isoo] Ham Sujeong?

999
00:55:43,465 --> 00:55:45,925
That name sounds familiar.

1000
00:55:45,926 --> 00:55:48,804
Ham Sujeong is...
[in English] "...Honey 7."

1001
00:55:49,763 --> 00:55:51,682
[in Korean] She's his only daughter,
born when he was 40.

1002
00:55:53,267 --> 00:55:54,350
[in English] Honey 7.

1003
00:55:54,351 --> 00:55:56,103
HONEY 7 HAM SUJEONG

1004
00:55:56,895 --> 00:55:58,187
[in Korean] We couldn't reach her.

1005
00:55:58,188 --> 00:56:00,983
Yes, she left for LA a week ago
and won't answer her phone.

1006
00:56:02,859 --> 00:56:05,403
His only daughter fell for a womanizer.

1007
00:56:05,404 --> 00:56:07,196
Of course he'd want to kill him.

1008
00:56:07,197 --> 00:56:10,200
Did he send his daughter to the US
and kill him while she was gone?

1009
00:56:13,870 --> 00:56:15,706
[taps table] I just got goosebumps.

1010
00:56:16,957 --> 00:56:20,001
His show was about Ham Sujeong.

1011
00:56:20,002 --> 00:56:23,422
There is someone I love.

1012
00:56:24,131 --> 00:56:25,715
She lived an unhappy life,

1013
00:56:25,716 --> 00:56:27,134
because her father

1014
00:56:28,552 --> 00:56:29,761
was a violent man.

1015
00:56:32,306 --> 00:56:35,057
[gasps] You're right. The violent father!

1016
00:56:35,058 --> 00:56:36,518
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

1017
00:56:37,394 --> 00:56:39,771
He saw the performance three days prior

1018
00:56:40,355 --> 00:56:43,317
and planned to use
the casket in his murder?

1019
00:56:49,364 --> 00:56:52,576
He snuck backstage
and poured kerosene inside the casket.

1020
00:56:53,410 --> 00:56:54,660
Would that be possible?

1021
00:56:54,661 --> 00:56:56,329
I think it's possible.

1022
00:56:56,330 --> 00:56:59,875
But why didn't he just kill Park Jaeha
when he took him three days ago?

1023
00:57:00,459 --> 00:57:02,169
He was making a statement.

1024
00:57:02,961 --> 00:57:05,380
"Are you saying my daughter is
unhappy because of me?"

1025
00:57:06,256 --> 00:57:08,758
"Then I'll kill you for real on stage."

1026
00:57:08,759 --> 00:57:12,053
[♪ music swells, fades]

1027
00:57:12,054 --> 00:57:14,180
I can't get a location on Ham Seongwook.

1028
00:57:14,181 --> 00:57:15,806
And he won't answer his phone.

1029
00:57:15,807 --> 00:57:17,434
Did you find out his address?

1030
00:57:18,060 --> 00:57:19,143
Yes.

1031
00:57:19,144 --> 00:57:22,147
IDENTITY RECORD
HAM SEONGWOOK

1032
00:57:23,065 --> 00:57:24,650
Let's go and see what happens.

1033
00:57:25,317 --> 00:57:27,401
Detective Choi,
send Dr. Yoon the autopsy request.

1034
00:57:27,402 --> 00:57:28,569
Got it.

1035
00:57:28,570 --> 00:57:29,737
Jin Isoo, come with me.

1036
00:57:29,738 --> 00:57:32,074
[♪ suspenseful, ticking music playing]

1037
00:57:35,619 --> 00:57:38,747
[engine purrs, brakes squeal]

1038
00:57:41,083 --> 00:57:43,001
[♪ rock music sting plays, fades]

1039
00:57:50,258 --> 00:57:52,886
[doorbell chiming]

1040
00:57:55,764 --> 00:57:57,973
[♪ suspenseful, foreboding music playing]

1041
00:57:57,974 --> 00:58:00,643
[doorbell chiming]

1042
00:58:00,644 --> 00:58:02,396
[Isoo] The lights are on.

1043
00:58:03,021 --> 00:58:04,648
[line connects, ringing]

1044
00:58:07,693 --> 00:58:08,944
[vehicle approaching]

1045
00:58:22,165 --> 00:58:23,166
[car door closes]

1046
00:58:24,918 --> 00:58:26,211
Can I help you?

1047
00:58:29,715 --> 00:58:30,840
Oh, oh, oh, oh, oh!

1048
00:58:30,841 --> 00:58:32,426
It's him. The guy who kicked my seat.

1049
00:58:33,051 --> 00:58:34,970
- [exclaiming]
- Let go.

1050
00:58:36,346 --> 00:58:38,056
[exclaims in pain]

1051
00:58:39,808 --> 00:58:40,933
[groans]

1052
00:58:40,934 --> 00:58:42,018
What do you want?

1053
00:58:42,728 --> 00:58:44,312
We're with the police.

1054
00:58:44,980 --> 00:58:46,231
- Him, too?
- [scoffs]

1055
00:58:47,315 --> 00:58:48,316
Uh...

1056
00:58:48,942 --> 00:58:50,026
Yes, police.

1057
00:58:59,369 --> 00:59:00,704
No need to make a fuss. Go inside.

1058
00:59:01,413 --> 00:59:02,414
[henchman] Yes, sir.

1059
00:59:03,540 --> 00:59:05,459
- Get moving.
- Get back inside.

1060
00:59:10,964 --> 00:59:12,048
What's your name?

1061
00:59:16,344 --> 00:59:19,013
DIRECTOR BAEK CHULMIN

1062
00:59:19,014 --> 00:59:20,348
Mr. Baek Chulmin.

1063
00:59:21,475 --> 00:59:23,435
You were there
on the day Mr. Park Jaeha died.

1064
00:59:24,644 --> 00:59:25,895
It was a spectacular show.

1065
00:59:25,896 --> 00:59:27,229
He burned pretty well.

1066
00:59:27,230 --> 00:59:29,023
[♪ music increases in tempo]

1067
00:59:29,024 --> 00:59:30,441
Did you kill him?

1068
00:59:30,442 --> 00:59:31,567
[chuckles]

1069
00:59:31,568 --> 00:59:32,860
[♪ music resumes tempo]

1070
00:59:32,861 --> 00:59:34,362
You're barking up the wrong tree.

1071
00:59:35,155 --> 00:59:38,241
If I'd killed him,
you would never have found the body.

1072
00:59:38,617 --> 00:59:39,784
Hey...

1073
00:59:39,785 --> 00:59:40,951
He's lying.

1074
00:59:40,952 --> 00:59:42,661
His eyes shifted.

1075
00:59:42,662 --> 00:59:43,913
They're shifting.

1076
00:59:43,914 --> 00:59:45,207
[♪ music swells, stops]

1077
00:59:46,082 --> 00:59:47,208
[♪ soft, suspenseful music playing]

1078
00:59:47,209 --> 00:59:49,585
Did you meet Mr. Park
three days before the incident?

1079
00:59:49,586 --> 00:59:52,254
- We had a chat.
- About what?

1080
00:59:52,255 --> 00:59:55,049
That bastard messed
with our boss's daughter.

1081
00:59:55,050 --> 00:59:57,928
So we just had a word with him.

1082
00:59:59,262 --> 01:00:02,766
Isn't it the Hammurabi way
to pay back in kind?

1083
01:00:03,183 --> 01:00:05,101
[scoffs] You've gone soft.

1084
01:00:06,102 --> 01:00:07,812
We need to meet Mr. Ham Seongwook.

1085
01:00:07,813 --> 01:00:09,439
- He's inside, right?
- The chairman

1086
01:00:10,440 --> 01:00:11,607
doesn't speak to cops.

1087
01:00:11,608 --> 01:00:12,733
[scoffs]

1088
01:00:12,734 --> 01:00:15,110
Everyone and their dog
is a chairman these days.

1089
01:00:15,111 --> 01:00:16,529
A chairman of what?

1090
01:00:16,530 --> 01:00:18,490
Of a <i>makgeolli</i> club? Huh?

1091
01:00:19,491 --> 01:00:20,699
What? Think I'm scared?

1092
01:00:20,700 --> 01:00:22,493
Let's end it here.

1093
01:00:22,494 --> 01:00:24,412
[♪ pulsating foreboding music playing]

1094
01:00:25,205 --> 01:00:26,414
[sighs in exasperation]

1095
01:00:29,042 --> 01:00:32,212
Move your car,
and teach your kid how to behave.

1096
01:00:34,464 --> 01:00:36,757
- Kid? You're calling me a kid?
- [♪ music fades]

1097
01:00:36,758 --> 01:00:37,968
- [scoffs]
- [gate closes]

1098
01:00:38,552 --> 01:00:41,221
He's proud of being a thug, is that it?

1099
01:00:42,013 --> 01:00:44,014
Acting all tough. [clicks tongue]

1100
01:00:44,015 --> 01:00:46,351
I think we need to meet Ham Seongwook.

1101
01:00:47,060 --> 01:00:48,143
Call him in.

1102
01:00:48,144 --> 01:00:49,270
[sighs]

1103
01:00:49,271 --> 01:00:50,313
Like he'd come.

1104
01:00:51,690 --> 01:00:52,691
[Isoo groans]

1105
01:00:54,317 --> 01:00:56,862
SEOUL GANGHA POLICE STATION

1106
01:00:59,948 --> 01:01:02,492
FATHER AND DAUGHTER
HONEY 7 HAM SUJEONG, HAM SEONGWOOK

1107
01:01:04,828 --> 01:01:06,037
You're all working hard.

1108
01:01:06,872 --> 01:01:09,331
Here's the file on Ham Seongwook.

1109
01:01:09,332 --> 01:01:10,791
Go pay him a visit.

1110
01:01:10,792 --> 01:01:12,001
Okay, thank you.

1111
01:01:12,002 --> 01:01:13,920
- Thank you, sir!
- Thank you, sir!

1112
01:01:14,421 --> 01:01:15,589
[door opens]

1113
01:01:16,548 --> 01:01:17,632
[door closes]

1114
01:01:19,718 --> 01:01:23,388
Do we really have to go this far
just to meet a mob boss?

1115
01:01:24,264 --> 01:01:26,724
If he's refusing to cooperate,
he's hiding something.

1116
01:01:26,725 --> 01:01:27,808
We need to meet him fast.

1117
01:01:27,809 --> 01:01:29,978
MOVEMENT REPORT

1118
01:01:31,605 --> 01:01:35,567
HERITAGE SHOOTING CLUB
WEEKLY VISIT EVERY WEDNESDAY

1119
01:01:36,234 --> 01:01:37,526
Tomorrow's Wednesday.

1120
01:01:37,527 --> 01:01:39,236
[♪ upbeat, jaunty music playing]

1121
01:01:39,237 --> 01:01:40,447
I'll arrange a meeting.

1122
01:01:41,865 --> 01:01:43,324
Jin Isoo, what's going on?

1123
01:01:43,325 --> 01:01:45,242
Just sit back and relax for now.

1124
01:01:45,243 --> 01:01:46,328
I'll let you know.

1125
01:01:48,204 --> 01:01:49,705
What's with him?

1126
01:01:49,706 --> 01:01:52,709
He's thought of a way.
We just need to wait.

1127
01:01:56,880 --> 01:01:57,881
[♪ music fades]

1128
01:01:59,090 --> 01:02:00,257
DETECTIVE JIN ISOO

1129
01:02:00,258 --> 01:02:01,885
[cell phone vibrating]

1130
01:02:04,429 --> 01:02:05,639
[groans softly]

1131
01:02:08,016 --> 01:02:09,183
[grunts]

1132
01:02:09,184 --> 01:02:10,936
[cell phone continues vibrating]

1133
01:02:12,187 --> 01:02:13,188
[exhales softly]

1134
01:02:14,397 --> 01:02:15,690
Detective Jin.

1135
01:02:16,983 --> 01:02:18,359
[Isoo] Mr. Choi, are you busy?

1136
01:02:18,360 --> 01:02:19,653
<i>No, I'm not.</i>

1137
01:02:20,195 --> 01:02:21,487
<i>What is it?</i>

1138
01:02:21,488 --> 01:02:22,948
I have a favor to ask.

1139
01:02:24,074 --> 01:02:25,367
All right.

1140
01:02:26,201 --> 01:02:28,202
I'll get it taken care of right away.

1141
01:02:28,203 --> 01:02:30,497
<i>Thank you. You're the best.</i>

1142
01:02:31,748 --> 01:02:32,791
[chuckles softly]

1143
01:02:33,291 --> 01:02:34,292
<i>Mr. Choi.</i>

1144
01:02:34,918 --> 01:02:36,001
Yes?

1145
01:02:36,002 --> 01:02:37,921
Why do you sound so down?

1146
01:02:38,588 --> 01:02:40,881
I don't sound down at all.

1147
01:02:40,882 --> 01:02:42,633
You're not unwell, are you?

1148
01:02:42,634 --> 01:02:44,135
I'm fine.

1149
01:02:45,053 --> 01:02:46,304
Don't worry.

1150
01:02:47,430 --> 01:02:48,848
Okay, I'll leave that with you.

1151
01:02:49,557 --> 01:02:50,642
[sighs softly]

1152
01:02:52,310 --> 01:02:53,687
- [line disconnects]
- [sighs weekly]

1153
01:02:54,938 --> 01:02:56,940
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

1154
01:03:11,579 --> 01:03:14,290
HERITAGE SHOOTING CLUB

1155
01:03:36,312 --> 01:03:38,773
I'm sorry, but we are
unable to accommodate you today.

1156
01:03:39,607 --> 01:03:40,692
What do you mean?

1157
01:03:41,443 --> 01:03:42,901
He comes here every Wednesday.

1158
01:03:42,902 --> 01:03:44,195
I'm really sorry.

1159
01:03:44,738 --> 01:03:48,199
The truth is, the owner told us
not to let anyone in today.

1160
01:03:48,992 --> 01:03:51,703
The owner? You mean Mr. Park?

1161
01:03:52,579 --> 01:03:54,038
[club manager] Well,

1162
01:03:54,039 --> 01:03:56,749
the owner has changed as of today.

1163
01:03:56,750 --> 01:03:58,001
The guy's got no manners.

1164
01:03:58,793 --> 01:04:00,711
- Who is it?
- [Isoo] It's me.

1165
01:04:00,712 --> 01:04:02,505
[♪ upbeat rock music playing]

1166
01:04:14,809 --> 01:04:16,186
[exhales smugly]

1167
01:04:16,561 --> 01:04:17,687
We finally get to meet.

1168
01:04:18,313 --> 01:04:19,773
Mr. Gangster, Ham Seongwook.

1169
01:04:22,776 --> 01:04:24,486
[♪ music swells]

1170
01:04:27,947 --> 01:04:29,282
[♪ music fades]

1171
01:04:31,284 --> 01:04:32,660
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

1172
01:04:39,918 --> 01:04:41,628
[♪ music increases in tempo]

1173
01:04:53,723 --> 01:04:55,016
[♪ music swells]

1174
01:04:59,562 --> 01:05:00,854
[gunshot]

1175
01:05:00,855 --> 01:05:02,397
[microphone feedback]

1176
01:05:02,398 --> 01:05:03,899
[♪ upbeat pop music playing,
Hersh "Shadows In The Night"]

1177
01:05:03,900 --> 01:05:05,192
FLEX X COP 2
EPISODE 7

1178
01:05:05,193 --> 01:05:06,486
A FACE-OFF WITH HAM SEONGWOOK!

1179
01:05:31,094 --> 01:05:34,514
Special Cast.
Son Woohyeon, Heo Sungtae, Jung Chaeyeon

1180
01:05:41,604 --> 01:05:43,814
- I won't ever see her again!
- Cut him.

1181
01:05:43,815 --> 01:05:45,024
[Sujeong] <i>Dad.</i>

1182
01:05:45,316 --> 01:05:46,317
Did you kill him?

1183
01:05:47,318 --> 01:05:48,986
Let's go back to the beginning.

1184
01:05:48,987 --> 01:05:50,279
[Kyungjin] <i>I know who bought the kerosene.</i>

1185
01:05:50,280 --> 01:05:51,405
[Hyera] <i>That's Ms. Lee Jiyun.</i>

1186
01:05:51,406 --> 01:05:53,699
[Junyoung] <i>There was a kerosene heater
in the workshop.</i>

1187
01:05:53,700 --> 01:05:55,909
[Hyera] <i>He wanted to kill his brother
out of jealousy?</i>

1188
01:05:55,910 --> 01:05:57,286
Were you in on it from the start?

1189
01:05:57,287 --> 01:05:59,414
- [Junyoung] Should start with this one.
- [Isoo, in English] Oh my god.

1190
01:05:59,998 --> 01:06:01,456
[in Korean] Pack up and leave quickly.

1191
01:06:01,457 --> 01:06:04,293
I can't return to the UK. [chuckles]

1192
01:06:04,294 --> 01:06:06,420
Two of Yu Seongwon's models disappeared.

1193
01:06:06,421 --> 01:06:08,839
- [bartender] Who is she?
- Someone obsessed with me.

1194
01:06:08,840 --> 01:06:11,675
<i>I'm thinking of using her as a model.</i>

1195
01:06:11,676 --> 01:06:13,552
[Isoo] <i>You just need to use me.</i>

1196
01:06:13,553 --> 01:06:15,638
<i>- I'll do anything you need.
-</i> [♪ music fades]

1197
01:06:18,057 --> 01:06:19,100
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

1198
01:06:31,279 --> 01:06:32,487
Seven women?

1199
01:06:32,488 --> 01:06:34,489
[inhales sharply, exhales]

1200
01:06:34,490 --> 01:06:35,574
Yes.

1201
01:06:35,575 --> 01:06:36,909
[scoffs]

1202
01:06:36,910 --> 01:06:38,203
My Sujeong...

1203
01:06:38,912 --> 01:06:40,079
is... [in English] "Honey 7"?

1204
01:06:45,543 --> 01:06:46,878
[♪ music swells]

1205
01:06:50,131 --> 01:06:51,673
- [in Korean] Go bring that bastard in.
- [♪ music fades]

1206
01:06:51,674 --> 01:06:52,926
Translated by Hyesoo Lee
